  "question": "Suppose $x,y\\in(0,\\pi/2)$ and $x\\ne y$. Which of the following statements is true?",
  "options": {
    "A": "$2\\sin(x+y)<\\sin2x+\\sin2y$ for all $x,y$;",
    "B": "$2\\sin(x+y)>\\sin2x+\\sin2y$ for all $x,y$;",
    "C": "There exist $x,y$ such that $2\\sin(x+y)=\\sin2x+\\sin2y$;",
    "D": "None of the above."
  },
  "answer": "B",
